       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is 5 times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg. Doses far above that raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, the effects could last for days.\n\nWas this meant to be one of these?\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg by mouth once daily**, which is sometimes used in frail patients or those with hepatic impairment. That doesn't apply to this patient.\n\nIf you do want 50 mg, please confirm it's intentional and tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
